LuauG: a lost D3D12 device crashes SDL_PushGPU*UniformData.

When the GPU is reset -- a shader that runs past the driver's timeout, TDR on
Windows, DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_HUNG -- every new resource fails. A uniform buffer
is one: D3D12_INTERNAL_AcquireUniformBufferFromPool returns NULL (it has set
the error), and D3D12_INTERNAL_PushUniformData dereferences it on the next
line. The application never learns the device is gone; it dies on an access
violation inside SDL.

The fix returns when there is no buffer, in both places one is acquired. The
data is dropped -- there is no device to draw it -- and the error stays set,
so the next call the application checks (a submit, a map, a create) fails and
says why. Found reproducing a hanging user shader (ADR 0091); still present
upstream on 2026-09-26.

diff --git a/src/gpu/d3d12/SDL_gpu_d3d12.c b/src/gpu/d3d12/SDL_gpu_d3d12.c
index fe69dd55..d4364e75 100644
--- a/src/gpu/d3d12/SDL_gpu_d3d12.c
+++ b/src/gpu/d3d12/SDL_gpu_d3d12.c
@@ -4686,6 +4686,13 @@ static void D3D12_INTERNAL_PushUniformData(
         return;
     }
 
+    // LuauG: a uniform buffer cannot be made once the device is lost (or out
+    // of memory); the error is already set, so drop the data rather than
+    // dereference NULL.
+    if (uniformBuffer == NULL) {
+        return;
+    }
+
     blockSize =
         D3D12_INTERNAL_Align(
             length,
@@ -4700,6 +4707,9 @@ static void D3D12_INTERNAL_PushUniformData(
         uniformBuffer->buffer->mapPointer = NULL;
 
         uniformBuffer = D3D12_INTERNAL_AcquireUniformBufferFromPool(commandBuffer);
+        if (uniformBuffer == NULL) {
+            return;
+        }
 
         uniformBuffer->drawOffset = 0;
         uniformBuffer->writeOffset = 0;
